# Godot 4+ specific ignores
.godot/

# Writable user:// root used by tools/verify.bat (shader cache, logs)
_userdata/

# Crash dumps produced by the local test harness
*.log
crash-*.txt

# Exported builds. export_presets.cfg writes to ../exe/Game.exe, but an old
# build was committed to the repository root and it is ~100 MB. Never commit
# build output: it bloats every clone forever and goes stale immediately.
/Game.exe
*.exe
*.pck
/export/
/exe/

# Third-party Steam emulators / DRM-bypass shims.
# These replace steam_api64.dll and fake ownership checks. They are not part of
# this project and must never enter the repo: test Steam with Valve's official
# public test AppID 480 (Spacewar) instead. See docs/MULTIPLAYER_PLAN.md.
steam_settings/
ColdClientLoader*
Goldberg*
SmartSteamEmu*

# GodotSteam GDExtension binaries. Installed by tools/setup_steam.bat, not committed.
#
# Why it is not in the repo:
#   * The full plugin is ~92 MB of prebuilt binaries (the Android build alone is
#     33 MB), against a 45 MB repository.
#   * Committing only win64 is worse than either extreme: the .gdextension lists
#     per-platform libraries, and Godot logs "No GDExtension library found for
#     current OS and architecture" when the running platform is missing. That
#     error would fail the headless audit on the Linux CI runner, which today
#     never sees the extension at all.
#   * A pinned download script is reproducible; a stale committed DLL is not.
#     The old committed copy was built for Godot 4.2 and had to be neutralised
#     with a .gdignore, which is exactly the trap this avoids.
addons/godotsteam/
